I come back into the flat and immediately open the backpack.
I am excited about my new things.
First, I try on the green jacket.
I look in the mirror.
The jacket is fantastic and fits perfectly.
It is light and very comfortable.
Then I take the yellow shirt out of the backpack.
I pull it over my head.
Oh no, that is difficult!
The shirt is much too tight across the shoulders.
I can hardly move my arms.
I take it off again immediately.
I compare it with my other shirts.
This shirt is definitely smaller than my other shirts.
Size M is normally exactly right for me.
But here I need size L.
I pack the shirt back into the backpack.
Fortunately, I still have the receipt.
I have to ride back to the shop and exchange the shirt.
